@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# T-055 — opus-4: main/boot near-misses + largest main drafts
+
+**8 functions MATCHED (6,216 B), 1 IMPROVED, 1 near-miss left UNCHANGED, 20 large drafts not attempted.** No commits.
+The ROM and all 3 images are byte-identical after a clean `make clean && make extract && make all && make progress`
+(ROM SHA1 ba52e91b…). Boot is now 100%.
+
+## Per-function results
+
+| Function | Result | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| func_8001CBCC | UNCHANGED (2 words) | See the finding below. The fix needs a new code subsegment, which is outside my yaml permission. |
+| func_80014250 | **MATCHED** | The T-045 draft (scalar `extern u8 D_1F…`, `(u32)&end - (s32)&start`) matches as-is in main_2FF0. The 3-word gap seen earlier came from different extern declarations. |
+| osPfsFileState (func_80035F10, main_265B0) | **MATCHED** | Verbatim ultralib pre-VERSION_J `pfsfilestate.c`: `start_page`/`bank` u8 locals with `bank` reassigned in the inner loop, and `int j`. No pad locals were needed. The TU now builds -O2 -mips1 (Makefile per-object CFLAGS line added). |
+| func_800249DC | **MATCHED** | The table is `struct {u8 id; u8 kind;} D_80046010[][7]`, searched with `for (i = 0; i < 7; i++) if (id == tbl[i].id) goto found; i = 0;`. |
+| boot func_80001564 | **MATCHED** | Verbatim gzip `inflate_fixed()`: the only change that mattered was `int i` (signed) with plain `for` loops. |
+| func_80018664 | **MATCHED** | A 40-entry 0x100-byte object array with an indexed loop (IDO unrolls it 2×). Keys: reuse one local `d` for both the cycle value and `obj->type`; `/ 256` and `* 256` integer divisors (no folding to `*1/256`); `vy += …`; `if (d >= 0) ad = d; else ad = -d;`. |
+| func_80016BE0 | **MATCHED** | A Vtx-style union (s64 alignment) gives lw/sw struct copies; `cn[0] = cn[1] = cn[2]` chain. Needed `D_8004AC89`/`D_8004AC8A` declared **u8** (with s8, IDO merges the constant 1 across the whole function). |
+| func_80016258 | **MATCHED** | Natural statement order. `D_80061520` declared **u8** with an `a[0] = a[1] = a[2] = a[3] = 20` chain. The D_80061CB8 bytes go after all D_800614D8 floats. Explicit `-= 2`/`--` loops over D_8004A730. |
+| func_80013CD8 | **MATCHED** | Natural `[0..3]` display order. The float/A998 block order was found by a hill-climb over statement groups: A740[0], zeros[0], A740[1], A998, A740[2], zeros[1], zeros[2], rot, speeds. Literals -3000/-2300 replace the late-rodata externs. |
+| func_80017378 | IMPROVED 463 → 41 | Exact up to 0x574 (natural order plus literals). The remaining words are all in the final 4-iteration A998/A9D8 loop: the original is a non-unrolled pointer loop that ends at the symbol D_8004AA14. It also needs D_8004A738 as u8; that change was **not** kept in src. Draft updated in place. |
+| func_80018664's hint D_800488CC | — | Removed the `force_migration function_owner:func_80018664` line. func_80018418 now uses the literal `650.0f` and the constant lands in the same pool slot (verified by the full build). |
+| func_800257FC, 80031DD0, 80015594, 8001C5AC, 800238C4, 80024CE0, 8001D7E4, 80014D5C, 800330B0, 80025FC4, 800306B8, 80020E98, 8001E33C, 800142E0, 8002E724, 80028A00, 80019880, 8000FA80, 8002BBD0, 8001EC74 | UNCHANGED (not attempted) | Out of time. All are display-list builders or FP-heavy logic. Their drafts screen at 343–600 words off in TU context (`ctx.py`). |
+
+## func_8001CBCC finding (not applied)
+D_80045C00 (0.017453292f) at image 0x362A0 is a **16-byte-padded block**. It sits between D_80045BEC (used by func_800193DC) and D_80045C10 (used by func_8001CD50). With the literal `0.017453292f` the function matches exactly. With any extern, defined, static, const or array form of D_80045C00 it stays 2 words off; -O3, -O1, -g3 and -mips1 don't help either.
+
